[32m+[m[32m### Free Sentinel-2 catalog discovery[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIn **Satellite data mode → Live Satellite**, search the official Copernicus Data Space Ecosystem (CDSE) STAC catalog for Sentinel-2 Level-2A items using a GeoJSON Polygon or MultiPolygon AOI, inclusive start/end dates, and maximum cloud-cover percentage. Search results are capped at 20 items per page and paginated with an opaque catalog cursor. Results include the stable STAC item ID, collection, acquisition time (UTC), cloud percentage, platform, product type/processing level, footprint/bounds when supplied, provider attribution, and the official catalog item link. Missing source metadata remains unavailable rather than being inferred.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe backend uses `https://stac.dataspace.copernicus.eu/v1/search` and fixes the collection to `sentinel-2-l2a`. The catalog search is public and requires no CDSE account or credentials; access to the app's API follows its configured Supabase authentication requirements. No catalog credentials or new dependencies are required. AOIs are validated and bounded (maximum 500 coordinates, existing 30-degree extent guard, and 1,000,000 km² area limit), and requests are sent only to the fixed official HTTPS endpoint with bounded timeouts and a 50-item hard result cap.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSelecting a result retains its provider, collection, stable item identifier, and catalog reference for a future acquisition handoff. It does not retrieve product assets, download full-resolution imagery, convert formats, or ingest data. To analyze imagery today, continue using the existing GeoTIFF upload and ingestion workflows.[m
